@flexiarg operator/approve-direction-with-amendments
@title Approve The Direction, Then Attach The Amendments
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-FiAUFY turn-m6cqV3
@parent orchestration/consent-gate
@context An agent has produced a draft (mockup, page, plan) and the operator is reviewing it in an iterative loop.

! conclusion: Open with a short directional approval ('Yeah something like this'), then list the concrete amendments; the approval licenses continued work, the amendments steer it.

  + IF:
    The overall direction is right but several details need changing.

  + HOWEVER:
    Silent edits read as rejection and stall the agent; full sign-off would endorse details that are wrong.

  + THEN:
    Open with a short directional approval ('Yeah something like this'), then list the concrete amendments; the approval licenses continued work, the amendments steer it.

  + BECAUSE:
    Consent-gate names the recorded approval locus from the acting side; this is the operator-side counterpart — the approval is recorded but scoped to direction, not detail, so the loop keeps moving without false sign-off.
